die@spammer.die (Mark Healey) writes:

> I got into a fight with a bunch of trolls and they kept coming back to
> life when there was a corpse left.  I had to keep killing them and
> running away until my cat got hungry enough to eat them.  I got bad.
> I was on the verge of eating them myself to deal with the situation.

So eat them!  Troll corpses don't have any harmful effects.  Or are
you playing a Monk?  They have a slight penalty for eating meat (1
point of alignment) which can safely be ignored.

> Is there a way to "kill" a corpse so that there isn't a chance of
> revivication?

Lots of ways:

* Let your pet eat it.
* Eat it yourself.
* Tin it.
* Polymorph the corpse.
* Polymorph the live troll.
* Throw it into water if it's not a water troll (it will drown when it
  revives).
* Put it in a box (I've heard rumours that trolls can break out of
  sacks in recent versions of NetHack).
* Just keep killing it until by chance it doesn't revive.

* Throw the corpse into lava?
* Bury the corpse?

(I don't remember seeing those last two in spoiler files, but they
sound logical.)

* Tame the live troll so that its resurrection ability becomes a good
  thing. :-)

Any other ways of permanently handling trolls?
